  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "In a nutrition study, the mass of bacteria in a culture (in $\\text{g}$) after $t$ hours is given by the function $M(t).$ The values of $M(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $1.5$ | $1.8$ | $2.1$ | $2.4$ | $2.7$ | $3.0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$M(t)$** | $6.2$ | $6.8$ | $7.5$ | $8.1$ | $8.7$ | $9.3$ |\n\nApproximate the bacteria’s mass instantaneous rate of change at $t=2.4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=0.3.$\n\nThe bacteria’s mass at $t=2.4$ is changing at approximately \n{{field-1}} $g$ per hour.",
